Original work
-------------

All source in `src/`, `tests/`, `udev/` and the build files is original to
this project.  There is no copied third-party source in this repository.

The CH32V00x erase and program sequence the flasher drives is the one
libopenwch's own `flash_common_v1.c` implements and the one WCH's EVT driver
uses, so the flasher and the library agree about the controller by
construction rather than by two independent readings of the reference manual.
The sequence is register writes over the debug interface; no target-side helper
program is uploaded, and therefore no vendor blob is embedded here.

The CH5xx families are erased and programmed by ROM routines reached through an
interface WCH does not document.  No sequence for them is implemented, and none
is guessed at.

The simulated programmer in `tests/` -- packet protocol, a subset of the RISC-V
instruction set, and the flash controller -- is likewise original work, written
from the same understanding as the code it exercises.  It exists so that a
whole flashing sequence can be run without a part attached; it can say nothing
about whether the parts behave as modelled.

Protocol knowledge, not code
----------------------------

The WCH-LinkE protocol is proprietary and undocumented by WCH.  It was
reverse-engineered by the community, and the following projects were consulted
to establish the **facts** of the interface — USB vendor and product
identifiers, the debug-register access shape, flash command sequencing, the
mode-switch mechanism.  Their source was read as documentation.  No code was
copied, and none of it is present here.

  minichlink (ch32fun)          https://github.com/cnlohr/ch32fun
                                MIT.  The most complete open implementation,
                                and the reference for which operations a
                                WCH-LinkE flasher has to perform.

  wlink                         https://github.com/Community-PIO-CH32V/wlink
                                and https://github.com/ch32-rs/wlink
                                Open-source WCH-Link libraries in Rust.

  riscv-openocd-wch             https://github.com/Seneral/riscv-openocd-wch
                                An OpenOCD fork with WCH-Link support.

  openocd-hacks                 https://github.com/karlp/openocd-hacks
                                Early notes on the DMI operations.

Register addresses, USB identifiers and command encodings are interface facts
and are not copyrightable expression.  This is the same position libopenwch
takes with respect to WCH's EVT packages, and it is recorded here for the same
reason: so a reader can tell what is original from what was learned elsewhere.

libusb
------

This program links against libusb, which is LGPL-2.1-or-later.  It is used as a
shared library and is not distributed here; the header is read from the system
or supplied by the user at build time.  No part of libusb is vendored into this
repository.

WCH's name and the WCH-LinkE are WCH's.  This project is not affiliated with or
endorsed by Nanjing Qinheng Microelectronics.
